  "title": "Multiple Myeloma (MM)",
  "summary": "Multiple Myeloma is diagnosed when a patient’s plasma cells grow uncontrolled. Plasma cells are a type of blood cell found in bone marrow that normally help fight infections by making antibodies. When there are too many plasma cells, they crowd out healthy blood cells and make abnormal proteins that impact bones, kidneys, and the immune system. Symptoms include […]",
